# Everything the image must never receive.
#
# node_modules is the big one: it is hundreds of megabytes, it is rebuilt inside
# the image by `npm ci` anyway, and copying a host-built tree in would ship
# whatever platform-specific binaries the developer's machine produced — a macOS
# arm64 esbuild binary does not run in a linux/amd64 container.

# --- Dependencies and build output ---------------------------------------
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.vite

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# .env carries build-time VITE_* values on a developer machine. The image gets
# its own, from the build argument — never a copy of someone's local file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Version control and tooling -----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.cursor

# --- Docs, CI and container files ----------------------------------------
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
guidelines/

# NOTE: Caddyfile is deliberately NOT ignored — the runtime stage copies it into
# the image. Excluding it fails the build with "/Caddyfile: not found".

# --- OS noise -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
